<Chapter id="services">
<h2>Sunken service routing</h2>
  <p>The routing header contains a four-bit service slot. Thus, one build can use
  at most 16 slot values. Each record carries the numeric slot, and build-specific
  constants assign readable service names.</p>

  <ServiceRegistryDiagram />

  <p>The wire route is <code>(direction, slot, command)</code>. The implementation
  keeps separate inbound and outbound code paths. Its inbound table looks up
  <code>(slot, command)</code>. Service names such as <code>Chat</code> are readable
  labels for the static slot values.</p>

  <h3 id="service-assignments">Service slots</h3>
  <p>The table matches the build-specific constants and dispatch tables. The
  directions show records that can currently be encoded or decoded.</p>
  <p>The table lists service records. Inbound command responses set the service
  flag to zero and use the fixed 16-bit layout.</p>

